    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d106">

                <pb facs="0165" n="73" sameAs="frus:frus1943CairoTehran/pg73"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt
                    Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Generalissimo
                        Chiang to President
                            Roosevelt</hi><anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d106-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-11-09">9 November 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Mme Chiang down with flu and dysentery.
                    Funeral of late President Lin Sen
                    scheduled for 17th. Provided Mme Chiang
                    has recovered I intend to leave here early on the 18th. Otherwise I must delay
                    my departure, in which case your conference with Stalin can take place before ours. I prefer seeing you before
                    you see Stalin and sincerely hope our
                    plans will work out in that way.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Chiang
                                Kai-shek</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d106-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d106-f1-content">
                <p>Sent by Stilwell, via Army channels, in
                    telegram 858, November 9, 1943, which was marked as “Secret”, “Priority”, and
                    “For the eyes of Gen Marshall only for
                    transmission to the President”.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
